## Engineering Project Manager

Pure Integration is a managed services company and system integrator serving cable and broadband service providers throughout the United States. We support our clients in all phases of their network design and evolution — from strategy to implementation.

We have an immediate opportunity for a Engineering Project Manager to join our Network Design & Engineering team. The candidate will be responsible for managing projects related to the following technologies/topics: Fiber to the Home (FTTH), Fiber to the Business (FTTB), Access Architecture (node splits), and Greenfield/Brownfield fiber deployments.

The candidate will provide project management leadership in developing the design, and prepare and deliver all types of construction drawings and permit packages. Candidate will be responsible for coordinating and managing local permit agencies and supporting construction crews with field surveys and as-built documentation. Candidate should be able to demonstrate the ability to identify and resolve design and engineering challenges with technical analysis. Basic understanding of fiber optic network design and routing, and knowledge of the following tools is a plus: Katapult Pro, AutoCAD, MicroStation, ArcGIS, or other applicable software.

Responsibilities:
- Manages and assigns work to drafters
- Reviews and approves all deliverables to be sent to clients
- Coordinate and communicate daily/weekly with clients
- Provide leadership within projects, demonstrating a strong attention to detail
- Strong writing skills for client deliverables, technical memos, and documentation
- Process incoming scoped tasks and manage team accordingly
- Manage subcontractors as needed
- Review field surveys and photos
- Process and review as-built documentation
- Perform field surveys as needed
- Process permit packages for clients to submit to local agencies
- Review drawings returned from permit agencies and provide updates/corrections
- Coordinate with permit agencies as needed

Requirements:
- 4+ years of experience in construction project management
- Ability to manage multiple projects simultaneously
- Strong attention to detail, problem-solving ability, and teamwork
- Experience with Microsoft Office (Teams, Excel, Word, Outlook) required
- Experience with Katapult Pro, AutoCAD, MicroStation, ArcGIS, or other applicable software preferred
- Ability to travel to job sites as needed
- Ability to pass a background check
- Drug free and fit for duty
- Reliable transportation

Salary: $70,000 - $95,000 per year
Benefits: Health, dental, vision, 401k
Clearance: None
Location: Remote

