Network Design & Engineering | Pure Integration

## Network Design & Engineering

Pure Integration provides network design and engineering services for cable and broadband service providers. Our team of experts uses the latest tools and techniques to design and optimize networks for maximum performance and reliability.

## OSP Engineering

Pure Integration supports the full lifecycle of Outside Plant (OSP) engineering services, including:
- Fiber route design and optimization
- Aerial and underground fiber design
- Construction drawing packages (CDPs)
- Permit packages for local jurisdictions
- Field verification and as-built documentation
- FTTH, FTTB, and backbone network design

## ISP Engineering

Pure Integration's ISP Engineering team focuses on network elements inside the facility or structure, providing the critical link between outside plant (OSP) and the subscriber:
- Riser and conduit system design
- Central Office (CO) or hub site design
- Equipment layout and placement plans
- ISP construction drawings and documentation

## Design Tools

Our engineering team leverages a combination of industry-standard tools and platforms:
- Katapult Pro for aerial and underground field data collection and design
- AutoCAD / MicroStation for construction drawing production
- ArcGIS for geospatial analysis and route planning
- Proprietary workflows for quality control and permit package preparation

## BEAD & Government Programs

Pure Integration actively supports broadband expansion programs, including BEAD-funded deployments. We help service providers navigate funding requirements, design eligible networks, and prepare compliant construction documentation for state broadband offices.

